[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1231957388","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605#issuecomment-1231957388","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605","id":1231957388,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85Jbi2M","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-30T17:27:42Z","updated_at":"2022-08-30T17:27:42Z","body":"There appear to be two key differences here:\r\n1) the name - which is already accommodated with markup.\r\n\r\n2) and the order (ish) of the first sentence:\r\n(Cornell version)\r\n\"Permission \r\nto use, copy, modify, and distribute this software and its documentation for any purpose, \r\nwithout fee, and without written agreement \r\nis hereby granted,\"\r\n\r\nv.\r\n(MIT-Modern-Variant)\r\n\"Permission is hereby granted, \r\nwithout written agreement and without license or royalty fees, \r\nto use, copy, modify, and distribute this software and its documentation for any purpose,\"\r\n\r\na) \"hereby granted\" is at the end v. beginning of the sentence - I can't see that that changes the meaning\r\nb) can we consider \"without fee, and without written agreement\" as legally substantively the same as \"without written agreement and without _license or royalty_ fees\"?\r\n\r\n@swinslow @pmadick - thoughts on this one?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1231957388/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1234928147","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605#issuecomment-1234928147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605","id":1234928147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85Jm4IT","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-02T00:06:47Z","updated_at":"2022-09-02T00:06:47Z","body":"@richardfontana - what is the priority on this one (and is there a corresponding Fedora Gitlab issue)?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1234928147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1234941236","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605#issuecomment-1234941236","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605","id":1234941236,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85Jm7U0","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-02T00:33:58Z","updated_at":"2022-09-02T00:33:58Z","body":"This is very low Fedora priority. There isn't even a Gitlab issue. It's a license that I discovered when trying to research some of the Callaway umbrella categories. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1234941236/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1236204726","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605#issuecomment-1236204726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605","id":1236204726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85Jrvy2","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-03T22:01:44Z","updated_at":"2022-09-03T22:01:44Z","body":"  > can we consider \"without fee, and without written agreement\" as legally substantively the same as \"without written agreement and without _license or royalty_ fees\"? \r\n\r\nObviously you can if you interpret \"fee\" in the first case as meaning \"license or royalty fees\". The \"without fee\" or similar language is a common element in this broad MIT/X-and-friends family of permissive FOSS licenses, and I would assume that a version with \"license or royalty fees\" was an attempt to clarify something that may have been thought to be unclear to one licensor. There are other FOSS licenses that have tried to explain the prohibitions on \"fees\" do not mean you can't \"sell (copies of the) software\". I seem to remember one license in this family that was problematic because the \"without fee\" was moved to a location in a sentence that made more plausible an interpretation that it was a prohibition on charging for distribution. Obviously such a prohibition is seen as conflicting with FOSS definitional norms, but those didn't exist before the development of most of these licenses. \r\n\r\nI would assume that SPDX can't say these licenses are substantively the same without engaging in some degree of legal interpretation (not sure if that goes against the \"just the facts\" principle). ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1236204726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1237420098","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605#issuecomment-1237420098","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605","id":1237420098,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85JwYhC","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-05T19:48:37Z","updated_at":"2022-09-05T19:48:37Z","body":"yeah, I feel like the variation make for very similar meaning in terms of general understanding, but is more specific as to the kind of fees in the one case, versus being open-ended as to just fees generally in the other.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1237420098/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1366065933","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605#issuecomment-1366065933","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605","id":1366065933,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85RbIMN","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-27T17:33:21Z","updated_at":"2022-12-27T17:33:21Z","body":"I tend to agree with @richardfontana and @jlovejoy that this warrants a new identifier.\r\n\r\nIt's actually (arguably) closer to [PostgreSQL](https://spdx.org/licenses/PostgreSQL.html) as @richardfontana mentioned, with the following differences:\r\n1. title, copyright lines and references to Cornell vs. Univ. of California (all already accommodated via markup)\r\n2. in paragraph 1: doesn't include \"and this paragraph\"\r\n3. in paragraph 1: adds \"of this software\" at the very end\r\n4. in paragraph 2: omits \"INCLUDING LOST PROFITS\" from the disclaimer\r\n5. in paragraph 3: \"OBLIGATIONS\" is singular in the last sentence\r\n\r\nOf these, I'd say that at least 2 and 4 would pass the extremely low bar that we usually use for saying \"these could arguably be substantively different.\" (If I was thinking about these for my personal use, I'd consider them essentially identical, but that isn't the test we use here.)  :)\r\n\r\nSo I'd be +1 to add as a separate license, probably with notes briefly indicating that it is very close to PostgreSQL.\r\n\r\nAs far as name / ID -- ugh, naming things is hard. I'd probably not just want to go with \"Cornell\" without more details. @richardfontana Do you happen to be able to point us to the package where this one was found?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1366065933/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1366103337","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605#issuecomment-1366103337","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605","id":1366103337,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85RbRUp","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-27T18:48:22Z","updated_at":"2022-12-27T18:48:22Z","body":"@swinslow  This tarball seems to contain the original lossless JPEG codec released under this license (with a couple of other licenses I had found in xmedcon including the old \"short\" IJG license):\r\nhttps://web.archive.org/web/20221025081849/http://www.dclunie.com/ljpegcornell/ljpg.tar.Z\r\n\r\nAll other uses of this license I found seem to point back to that release, e.g.:\r\nhttps://mipav.cit.nih.gov/license/CopyrightInfo.html#source-dicomcomm \r\nhttps://mipav.cit.nih.gov/documentation/api/gov/nih/mipav/model/file/FileDicomJPEG.html\r\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/dng_sdk/+/refs/heads/master/source/dng_lossless_jpeg.cpp#16 (code from some Adobe software; uses \"Cornell\" rather than \"the Cornell\")\r\nhttps://www.mssl.ucl.ac.uk/~mcrw/src/20050920/proto.h\r\nhttps://help.landscapepro.pics/v3-third-party-credits/\r\nhttps://gitlab.freedesktop.org/libopenraw/libopenraw/blob/master/lib/ljpegdecompressor.cpp#L32\r\n \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1366103337/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1431487790","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605#issuecomment-1431487790","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605","id":1431487790,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85VUsUu","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-02-15T14:48:42Z","updated_at":"2023-02-15T14:48:42Z","body":"@richardfontana So, interestingly, here's what I'm seeing as the corresponding license text in that .Z file linked in the prior comment:\r\n\r\n```\r\nCopyright (c) 1993 Cornell University, Kongji Huang\r\nAll rights reserved.\r\n\r\nPermission to use, copy, modify, and distribute this software and its\r\ndocumentation for research purposes, without fee, and without written\r\nagreement is hereby granted, provided that the above copyright notice\r\nand the following two paragraphs appear in all copies of this\r\nsoftware.\r\n\r\nIN NO EVENT SHALL THE CORNELL UNIVERSITY BE LIABLE TO ANY PARTY FOR\r\nDIRECT, INDIRECT, SPECIAL, INCIDENTAL, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES ARISING\r\nOUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE AND ITS DOCUMENTATION, EVEN IF THE\r\nUNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA HAS BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH\r\nDAMAGE.\r\n\r\nTHE CORNELL UNIVERSITY SPECIFICALLY DISCLAIMS ANY WARRANTIES,\r\nINCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF\r\nMERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  THE SOFTWARE\r\nPROVIDED HEREUNDER IS ON AN \"AS IS\" BASIS, AND THE UNIVERSITY OF\r\nCALIFORNIA HAS NO OBLIGATION TO PROVIDE MAINTENANCE, SUPPORT, UPDATES,\r\nENHANCEMENTS, OR MODIFICATIONS.\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhich looks very close to the text for this thread, but there's two differences, one of which matters:\r\n* in the first sentence, instead of permission being granted \"for any purposes\", it is granted \"for research purposes\"\r\n* in the second and third paragraphs, someone got confused when replacing university names (sometimes it's Cornell, sometimes it's University of California)\r\n\r\nThe first one of course is the issue -- this appears to limit use to \"research purposes\".\r\n\r\nFor the subsequent links you provided, the first two include the \"research purposes\" limitation, the remaining four are the \"any purposes\" version.\r\n\r\nI'm assuming that the version Fedora is using is the \"any purposes\" text that is provided at the top of this issue?\r\n\r\nIf so, I'm +1 to add it as a new license, perhaps with the following:\r\n* ID: `Cornell-Lossless-JPEG`\r\n* Name: Cornell Lossless JPEG License\r\n\r\nand if someone comes along and wants the \"research purposes\" version later on, then we can figure out a separate ID and name for it. How does that sound?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1431487790/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1433902577","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605#issuecomment-1433902577","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1605","id":1433902577,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85Vd53x","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-02-16T23:59:23Z","updated_at":"2023-02-16T23:59:23Z","body":"that sounds like a good approach, but I'd like to hear what @richardfontana  thinks","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1433